  "observations": [
    "Equal-width/context-on emitted one context_leakage warning on ew-03, then returned the correct current-cue translation in 1260 ms. Raw rejected output is not published, so this is a suspected-replay recovery observation, not a semantic proof of the rejected answer.",
    "Negative recovery/context-on emitted timeout and context_degraded warnings for nb-dialogue-05; recovery succeeded at 4349 ms. Its five-sample p95 was 3636.8 ms. This is functional recovery evidence, not a tail-latency improvement claim.",
    "Both negative runs admitted the initial authored watermark during the allowed warmup. Zero post-warmup admissions does not imply that bandHeld always clears an earlier overlay.",
    "An initial equal-width/context-off attempt produced 30 translations but the report counted 29 because the first capture preceded the fixture clock by 224 ms. That attempt is excluded; starting the fixture before capture produced the complete 30/30 result without changing report rules.",
    "An earlier interrupted run is excluded. The accepted context-on equal-width run initially had the fixture above the overlay; removing topmost exposed the overlay, and its later native screenshot was inspected. Subsequent runs kept the fixture non-topmost.",
    "One 120-second cycle per final case on one ARM64 CPU host. No native x64, GPU, Linux capture, installer, or sustained multi-cycle claim. The replay guard is lexical and cannot detect every semantic leak."
  ],
